1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,193
Sweetheart, my cousin Marjorie owned thirty-one grocery

2
00:00:04,193 --> 00:00:05,642
stores across Ohio.

3
00:00:05,822 --> 00:00:08,129
And at seventy-six years old,

4
00:00:08,129 --> 00:00:10,435
she put on a gray uniform and

5
00:00:10,435 --> 00:00:12,662
a name tag that said Margie,

6
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:15,367
and took a job cleaning the floors

7
00:00:15,367 --> 00:00:17,275
at her own headquarters,

8
00:00:17,275 --> 00:00:20,218
at night, for eleven dollars an hour.

9
00:00:20,398 --> 00:00:23,150
Not one person in that building knew

10
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:24,067
who she was.

11
00:00:24,247 --> 00:00:26,370
She was looking for the person who

12
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:28,556
would run her company after she was

13
00:00:28,556 --> 00:00:28,868
gone.

14
00:00:29,218 --> 00:00:31,372
Tonight I'm going to tell you what

15
00:00:31,372 --> 00:00:33,272
Marjorie saw with a mop in her

16
00:00:33,272 --> 00:00:35,617
hand, the vice president who made her

17
00:00:35,617 --> 00:00:37,264
clean up his coffee twice,

18
00:00:37,264 --> 00:00:39,355
and the young woman from the mail

19
00:00:39,355 --> 00:00:41,445
room who did one small thing that

20
00:00:41,445 --> 00:00:42,523
changed her life.

21
00:00:42,703 --> 00:00:43,663
Stay with me,

22
00:00:43,663 --> 00:00:46,545
honey, because the board meeting at the

23
00:00:46,545 --> 00:00:48,688
end of this story is the most

24
00:00:48,688 --> 00:00:51,422
satisfying thing I've ever witnessed.

25
00:00:51,772 --> 00:00:54,457
Marjorie and I grew up together in

26
00:00:54,457 --> 00:00:56,195
Mansfield, sweetheart.

27
00:00:56,375 --> 00:00:58,546
Our mothers were sisters.

28
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:00,287
In nineteen sixty-two,

29
00:01:00,287 --> 00:01:02,843
she and her husband Frank opened one

30
00:01:02,843 --> 00:01:05,469
little grocery store on the corner of

31
00:01:05,469 --> 00:01:06,605
Fourth and Main,

32
00:01:06,605 --> 00:01:09,302
with a cash register Frank bought used

33
00:01:09,302 --> 00:01:11,857
and a sign Marjorie painted herself.

34
00:01:12,037 --> 00:01:14,359
They worked sixteen hours a day.

35
00:01:14,539 --> 00:01:17,926
Marjorie knew every customer's name and every

36
00:01:17,926 --> 00:01:19,206
child's birthday.

37
00:01:19,556 --> 00:01:21,257
By the time Frank died,

38
00:01:21,257 --> 00:01:23,402
there were thirty-one stores,

39
00:01:23,402 --> 00:01:25,103
two thousand employees,

40
00:01:25,103 --> 00:01:28,062
and a big glass headquarters building in

41
00:01:28,062 --> 00:01:28,727
Columbus.

42
00:01:28,907 --> 00:01:30,881
And Marjorie had a problem.

43
00:01:31,061 --> 00:01:32,536
She had no children.

44
00:01:32,716 --> 00:01:35,218
And she had three vice presidents,

45
00:01:35,218 --> 00:01:36,542
all in fine suits,

46
00:01:36,542 --> 00:01:38,235
all very polite to her,

47
00:01:38,235 --> 00:01:40,810
all telling her they were the right

48
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:42,723
person to run the company.

49
00:01:42,903 --> 00:01:45,246
In a minute I'll tell you which

50
00:01:45,246 --> 00:01:46,607
one she suspected.

51
00:01:46,957 --> 00:01:48,229
She said to me,

52
00:01:48,229 --> 00:01:51,030
Ruth, every one of them smiles at

53
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:52,727
me in the boardroom.

54
00:01:52,907 --> 00:01:54,318
But Frank always said,

55
00:01:54,318 --> 00:01:56,435
you don't know a man until you've

56
00:01:56,435 --> 00:01:58,553
seen how he treats the people who

57
00:01:58,553 --> 00:02:00,221
can't do anything for him.

58
00:02:00,401 --> 00:02:01,948
And in that building,

59
00:02:01,948 --> 00:02:05,115
I'm the one everybody wants something from.

60
00:02:05,295 --> 00:02:07,682
I'll never see the truth from the

61
00:02:07,682 --> 00:02:08,406
top floor.

62
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:10,271
I have to see it from the

63
00:02:10,271 --> 00:02:10,676
floor.

64
00:02:11,025 --> 00:02:12,236
So she did it,

65
00:02:12,236 --> 00:02:12,755
honey.

66
00:02:12,935 --> 00:02:14,719
She told the board she was going

67
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:16,279
to Florida for three months.

68
00:02:16,459 --> 00:02:18,654
She dyed her white hair brown,

69
00:02:18,654 --> 00:02:20,922
put on glasses she didn't need,

70
00:02:20,922 --> 00:02:23,555
and applied for a night cleaning job

71
00:02:23,555 --> 00:02:24,872
through an agency,

72
00:02:24,872 --> 00:02:27,140
under her mother's maiden name.

73
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,458
Margie Holt.

74
00:02:28,638 --> 00:02:31,437
Nobody at headquarters had seen her in

75
00:02:31,437 --> 00:02:33,572
person more than a few times.

76
00:02:33,752 --> 00:02:35,742
She walked right in and got a

77
00:02:35,742 --> 00:02:36,016
mop.

78
00:02:36,366 --> 00:02:38,631
She worked from six at night until

79
00:02:38,631 --> 00:02:39,896
two in the morning.

80
00:02:40,076 --> 00:02:42,270
Emptying trash cans.

81
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:44,064
Vacuuming offices.

82
00:02:44,244 --> 00:02:45,846
Cleaning bathrooms.

83
00:02:46,026 --> 00:02:48,698
And she said the strangest thing happened

84
00:02:48,698 --> 00:02:50,066
the very first night.

85
00:02:50,246 --> 00:02:51,907
She became invisible.

86
00:02:52,087 --> 00:02:54,416
People walked past her like she was

87
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:55,813
a piece of furniture.

88
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:59,295
They talked on their phones about everything,

89
00:02:59,295 --> 00:03:00,909
right in front of her,

90
00:03:00,909 --> 00:03:02,669
as if she couldn't hear.

91
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:04,797
And she learned things,

92
00:03:04,797 --> 00:03:05,260
honey.

93
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,611
Things no report ever told her.

94
00:03:07,791 --> 00:03:10,313
That the heat in the warehouse office

95
00:03:10,313 --> 00:03:12,493
had been broken for two winters.

96
00:03:12,673 --> 00:03:15,696
That the night security guard was working

97
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,792
two jobs because his wife needed dialysis.

98
00:03:18,972 --> 00:03:21,022
That the coffee in the break room

99
00:03:21,022 --> 00:03:23,073
was paid for by the cleaning crew

100
00:03:23,073 --> 00:03:24,626
out of their own pockets.

101
00:03:24,806 --> 00:03:26,523
She wrote it all down in a

102
00:03:26,523 --> 00:03:29,032
little notebook in her uniform pocket.

103
00:03:29,381 --> 00:03:31,998
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

104
00:03:31,998 --> 00:03:34,016
tap the like button for me,

105
00:03:34,016 --> 00:03:34,838
sweetheart.

106
00:03:35,018 --> 00:03:38,315
It helps more people find these stories.

107
00:03:38,495 --> 00:03:41,130
The first vice president was a man

108
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:42,060
named Grant.

109
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:46,141
Tall, handsome, always smiling in meetings.

110
00:03:46,321 --> 00:03:49,668
One night, Marjorie was mopping outside his

111
00:03:49,668 --> 00:03:52,159
office, and he walked out with a

112
00:03:52,159 --> 00:03:53,638
full cup of coffee,

113
00:03:53,638 --> 00:03:55,740
bumped into her mop bucket,

114
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:58,309
and spilled it all over the floor

115
00:03:58,309 --> 00:03:59,788
she'd just cleaned.

116
00:04:00,139 --> 00:04:01,943
He didn't say sorry,

117
00:04:01,943 --> 00:04:02,484
honey.

118
00:04:02,664 --> 00:04:04,420
He looked down at it,

119
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:05,423
then at her,

120
00:04:05,423 --> 00:04:06,427
and he said,

121
00:04:06,427 --> 00:04:08,852
well, don't just stand there.

122
00:04:09,032 --> 00:04:10,845
Then he got a second cup,

123
00:04:10,845 --> 00:04:12,295
and on his way back,

124
00:04:12,295 --> 00:04:14,688
he dropped the empty cup right on

125
00:04:14,688 --> 00:04:16,791
the floor next to her bucket,

126
00:04:16,791 --> 00:04:18,169
and walked over it.

127
00:04:18,349 --> 00:04:19,696
On purpose.

128
00:04:19,876 --> 00:04:21,904
She heard him on the phone a

129
00:04:21,904 --> 00:04:23,426
minute later, saying,

130
00:04:23,426 --> 00:04:25,309
the old lady's in Florida.

131
00:04:25,489 --> 00:04:27,042
Once the board votes,

132
00:04:27,042 --> 00:04:29,631
I'm cutting the night staff to save

133
00:04:29,631 --> 00:04:30,075
money.

134
00:04:30,424 --> 00:04:33,234
The second vice president was a woman

135
00:04:33,234 --> 00:04:34,221
named Lauren.

136
00:04:34,401 --> 00:04:36,700
She never spilled anything.

137
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,122
She was polite.

138
00:04:38,302 --> 00:04:39,795
But in three months,

139
00:04:39,795 --> 00:04:42,408
she never once said good evening to

140
00:04:42,408 --> 00:04:45,245
Margie, never once looked at her face.

141
00:04:45,425 --> 00:04:46,434
And one night,

142
00:04:46,434 --> 00:04:49,461
Marjorie heard her tell another manager to

143
00:04:49,461 --> 00:04:51,983
fire a cashier at the Dayton store,

144
00:04:51,983 --> 00:04:54,578
a single mother who'd been late four

145
00:04:54,578 --> 00:04:56,884
times because her baby was sick.

146
00:04:57,064 --> 00:04:59,873
Lauren said, rules are rules.

147
00:05:00,053 --> 00:05:02,248
Sentiment is expensive.

148
00:05:02,598 --> 00:05:04,641
The third vice president,

149
00:05:04,641 --> 00:05:06,765
Doug, was friendly enough.

150
00:05:06,945 --> 00:05:08,652
He'd say, evening,

151
00:05:08,652 --> 00:05:09,221
ma'am.

152
00:05:09,401 --> 00:05:10,859
But one Friday night,

153
00:05:10,859 --> 00:05:13,637
Marjorie overheard him on the phone with

154
00:05:13,637 --> 00:05:16,276
a supplier, and she realized he'd been

155
00:05:16,276 --> 00:05:18,429
taking money on the side to put

156
00:05:18,429 --> 00:05:20,860
their products on the best shelves.

157
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:23,207
Twenty years with the company,

158
00:05:23,207 --> 00:05:23,641
honey.

159
00:05:23,821 --> 00:05:26,121
And he'd been stealing from her and

160
00:05:26,121 --> 00:05:27,501
Frank the whole time.

161
00:05:27,851 --> 00:05:30,173
So far, three vice presidents,

162
00:05:30,173 --> 00:05:32,572
and not one of them she'd trust

163
00:05:32,572 --> 00:05:34,120
with a single store.

164
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,890
Marjorie came to my house that Sunday

165
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:38,990
and cried at my kitchen table.

166
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:40,503
She said, Ruth,

167
00:05:40,503 --> 00:05:43,436
Frank and I built that place with

168
00:05:43,436 --> 00:05:44,325
our hands.

169
00:05:44,505 --> 00:05:46,452
And the people at the top are

170
00:05:46,452 --> 00:05:48,534
the worst ones in the building.

171
00:05:48,714 --> 00:05:50,027
And then she said,

172
00:05:50,027 --> 00:05:52,216
but there's a girl in the mail

173
00:05:52,216 --> 00:05:54,623
room I can't stop thinking about.

174
00:05:54,974 --> 00:05:56,808
Her name was Rosa.

175
00:05:56,988 --> 00:05:58,292
She was twenty-six,

176
00:05:58,292 --> 00:06:00,693
she sorted mail on the first floor,

177
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:03,095
and she was taking night classes in

178
00:06:03,095 --> 00:06:05,428
business at the community college.

179
00:06:05,608 --> 00:06:07,851
She studied at the little table by

180
00:06:07,851 --> 00:06:10,555
the vending machines on her dinner break,

181
00:06:10,555 --> 00:06:12,467
at eight o'clock every night,

182
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:15,105
right where Marjorie took her break too.

183
00:06:15,285 --> 00:06:17,508
And the very first night,

184
00:06:17,508 --> 00:06:20,708
Rosa looked up from her textbook and

185
00:06:20,708 --> 00:06:21,508
said, hi.

186
00:06:21,688 --> 00:06:22,907
I'm Rosa.

187
00:06:23,087 --> 00:06:24,539
What's your name?

188
00:06:24,889 --> 00:06:26,835
Every night after that,

189
00:06:26,835 --> 00:06:28,697
Rosa saved her a seat.

190
00:06:28,877 --> 00:06:31,164
She asked about Margie's family.

191
00:06:31,344 --> 00:06:33,129
She shared her dinner,

192
00:06:33,129 --> 00:06:35,157
rice and beans from home,

193
00:06:35,157 --> 00:06:37,834
because Margie only had crackers.

194
00:06:38,014 --> 00:06:40,443
She told Margie about her mother,

195
00:06:40,443 --> 00:06:43,240
who cleaned houses in Columbus and had

196
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,933
raised four kids alone.

197
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,037
And she said,

198
00:06:46,037 --> 00:06:47,386
my mom always says,

199
00:06:47,386 --> 00:06:50,086
the people who clean the building know

200
00:06:50,086 --> 00:06:52,430
more about it than the people who

201
00:06:52,430 --> 00:06:52,927
own it.

202
00:06:53,277 --> 00:06:56,066
And then, the small thing I promised

203
00:06:56,066 --> 00:06:56,376
you.

204
00:06:56,556 --> 00:06:58,299
One night in December,

205
00:06:58,299 --> 00:06:59,884
it was snowing hard,

206
00:06:59,884 --> 00:07:01,943
and the buses had stopped.

207
00:07:02,123 --> 00:07:04,576
Margie was standing at the door at

208
00:07:04,576 --> 00:07:05,947
two in the morning,

209
00:07:05,947 --> 00:07:07,174
with no way home.

210
00:07:07,354 --> 00:07:09,711
Rosa had stayed late to study.

211
00:07:09,891 --> 00:07:12,442
She saw her standing there in her

212
00:07:12,442 --> 00:07:14,297
thin coat, and she said,

213
00:07:14,297 --> 00:07:16,462
Margie, I'll drive you home.

214
00:07:16,642 --> 00:07:18,012
Where do you live?

215
00:07:18,192 --> 00:07:19,854
And Marjorie panicked,

216
00:07:19,854 --> 00:07:22,197
because she lived in a mansion.

217
00:07:22,548 --> 00:07:25,080
So Marjorie gave her my address,

218
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:25,555
honey.

219
00:07:25,735 --> 00:07:26,919
In Mansfield.

220
00:07:27,099 --> 00:07:29,154
An hour away in the snow.

221
00:07:29,334 --> 00:07:30,924
Rosa didn't blink.

222
00:07:31,104 --> 00:07:33,273
She drove an old Honda with a

223
00:07:33,273 --> 00:07:35,217
heater that barely worked,

224
00:07:35,217 --> 00:07:36,488
an hour each way,

225
00:07:36,488 --> 00:07:38,133
at two in the morning,

226
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:39,254
in a snowstorm.

227
00:07:39,434 --> 00:07:41,783
And when she dropped Margie off at

228
00:07:41,783 --> 00:07:44,476
my door, she pressed something into her

229
00:07:44,476 --> 00:07:44,821
hand.

230
00:07:45,001 --> 00:07:46,940
It was twenty dollars.

231
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,222
She said, for groceries.

232
00:07:49,402 --> 00:07:51,747
I know cleaning doesn't pay much.

233
00:07:52,097 --> 00:07:53,942
Twenty dollars, sweetheart.

234
00:07:54,122 --> 00:07:56,816
From a girl making fourteen dollars an

235
00:07:56,816 --> 00:07:58,587
hour, with student loans,

236
00:07:58,587 --> 00:08:00,926
sending money home to her mother.

237
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:03,762
Marjorie came into my kitchen at three

238
00:08:03,762 --> 00:08:04,810
in the morning,

239
00:08:04,810 --> 00:08:07,467
still holding that twenty-dollar bill,

240
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,633
and she sat down and didn't say

241
00:08:09,633 --> 00:08:11,381
anything for a long time.

242
00:08:11,561 --> 00:08:13,325
And then she said,

243
00:08:13,325 --> 00:08:15,090
Ruth, I found her.

244
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:16,541
And I said,

245
00:08:16,541 --> 00:08:17,697
found who?

246
00:08:17,877 --> 00:08:18,849
And she said,

247
00:08:18,849 --> 00:08:21,244
the one Frank would have picked.

248
00:08:21,594 --> 00:08:23,594
For the rest of the winter,

249
00:08:23,594 --> 00:08:25,817
Marjorie watched Rosa closely,

250
00:08:25,817 --> 00:08:26,632
sweetheart.

251
00:08:26,812 --> 00:08:29,005
She saw her help a lost delivery

252
00:08:29,005 --> 00:08:30,992
driver find the loading dock.

253
00:08:31,172 --> 00:08:33,204
She saw her stay late to fix

254
00:08:33,204 --> 00:08:35,743
a mistake somebody else had made in

255
00:08:35,743 --> 00:08:36,396
the mail.

256
00:08:36,576 --> 00:08:38,572
She saw her give her umbrella to

257
00:08:38,572 --> 00:08:39,757
the security guard.

258
00:08:39,937 --> 00:08:41,016
And not once,

259
00:08:41,016 --> 00:08:42,344
in three months,

260
00:08:42,344 --> 00:08:44,751
did Rosa ever do a kind thing

261
00:08:44,751 --> 00:08:47,739
when anybody important was watching.

262
00:08:47,919 --> 00:08:50,125
There was nobody important there.

263
00:08:50,305 --> 00:08:51,861
Just Margie.

264
00:08:52,211 --> 00:08:55,055
In March, Marjorie came back from Florida,

265
00:08:55,055 --> 00:08:57,359
with her white hair and her pearls

266
00:08:57,359 --> 00:08:58,578
and her good suit,

267
00:08:58,578 --> 00:09:00,813
and called a meeting of the board

268
00:09:00,813 --> 00:09:02,845
and all three vice presidents.

269
00:09:03,025 --> 00:09:03,953
I was there,

270
00:09:03,953 --> 00:09:05,498
sitting in the back,

271
00:09:05,498 --> 00:09:07,739
because she asked me to come.

272
00:09:07,919 --> 00:09:09,544
Grant was smiling.

273
00:09:09,724 --> 00:09:11,396
Lauren had a folder.

274
00:09:11,576 --> 00:09:13,445
Doug was sweating a little.

275
00:09:13,625 --> 00:09:15,759
Each of them thought they were about

276
00:09:15,759 --> 00:09:17,596
to be named the next president.

277
00:09:17,946 --> 00:09:20,319
Marjorie stood up at the head of

278
00:09:20,319 --> 00:09:22,174
that long table and said,

279
00:09:22,174 --> 00:09:23,658
I wasn't in Florida.

280
00:09:23,838 --> 00:09:24,919
For three months,

281
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:27,019
I cleaned this building at night.

282
00:09:27,199 --> 00:09:29,392
And she put a gray uniform on

283
00:09:29,392 --> 00:09:31,736
the table, with a name tag that

284
00:09:31,736 --> 00:09:32,644
said Margie.

285
00:09:32,824 --> 00:09:35,750
Grant's face went the color of paste.

286
00:09:35,930 --> 00:09:37,996
Lauren dropped her pen.

287
00:09:38,176 --> 00:09:39,326
And Doug, honey,

288
00:09:39,326 --> 00:09:41,555
Doug looked at the door like he

289
00:09:41,555 --> 00:09:43,784
was planning to run through it.

290
00:09:44,134 --> 00:09:46,298
She looked at Grant and said,

291
00:09:46,298 --> 00:09:48,986
you spilled coffee on my clean floor

292
00:09:48,986 --> 00:09:51,151
and told me not to just stand

293
00:09:51,151 --> 00:09:51,599
there.

294
00:09:51,779 --> 00:09:53,704
And then you threw your cup at

295
00:09:53,704 --> 00:09:54,217
my feet.

296
00:09:54,397 --> 00:09:55,987
Grant, you're done.

297
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,535
She looked at Lauren and said,

298
00:09:58,535 --> 00:10:01,218
the cashier in Dayton gets her job

299
00:10:01,218 --> 00:10:02,797
back, with back pay.

300
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:05,212
And you can find a company where

301
00:10:05,212 --> 00:10:07,238
sentiment isn't so expensive.

302
00:10:07,418 --> 00:10:10,268
And then she handed Doug an envelope

303
00:10:10,268 --> 00:10:12,248
from the company lawyers,

304
00:10:12,248 --> 00:10:14,702
and said, I think you know what

305
00:10:14,702 --> 00:10:15,336
this is.

306
00:10:15,686 --> 00:10:18,209
Then Marjorie pressed a button on the

307
00:10:18,209 --> 00:10:19,232
phone and said,

308
00:10:19,232 --> 00:10:20,051
send her up.

309
00:10:20,231 --> 00:10:22,450
And the boardroom door opened,

310
00:10:22,450 --> 00:10:24,670
and in came Rosa from the mail

311
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:26,519
room, in her best blouse,

312
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:27,703
scared to death,

313
00:10:27,703 --> 00:10:30,440
because nobody from the mail room had

314
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:32,955
ever been called to the top floor.

315
00:10:33,135 --> 00:10:35,029
She looked around that room,

316
00:10:35,029 --> 00:10:37,193
and she saw Marjorie at the head

317
00:10:37,193 --> 00:10:38,749
of the table in pearls,

318
00:10:38,749 --> 00:10:39,628
and she said,

319
00:10:39,628 --> 00:10:40,101
Margie?

320
00:10:40,452 --> 00:10:43,293
Marjorie walked around that table and gave

321
00:10:43,293 --> 00:10:45,525
Rosa back her twenty-dollar bill.

322
00:10:45,705 --> 00:10:47,837
Then she told the board that the

323
00:10:47,837 --> 00:10:50,036
company would pay for the rest of

324
00:10:50,036 --> 00:10:53,035
Rosa's college, and her master's degree after

325
00:10:53,035 --> 00:10:53,368
that.

326
00:10:53,548 --> 00:10:56,137
And that Rosa would spend the next

327
00:10:56,137 --> 00:10:58,422
five years working beside her,

328
00:10:58,422 --> 00:11:00,021
learning every store,

329
00:11:00,021 --> 00:11:02,687
every job, from the loading dock to

330
00:11:02,687 --> 00:11:03,753
the boardroom.

331
00:11:03,933 --> 00:11:05,848
And then she'd be president.

332
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:08,574
Rosa has run that company for six

333
00:11:08,574 --> 00:11:10,158
years now, sweetheart.

334
00:11:10,338 --> 00:11:12,195
Thirty-eight stores.

335
00:11:12,375 --> 00:11:14,959
She raised the night cleaning staff's pay

336
00:11:14,959 --> 00:11:15,905
the first week.

337
00:11:16,085 --> 00:11:17,661
And every new manager,

338
00:11:17,661 --> 00:11:18,951
before they start,

339
00:11:18,951 --> 00:11:21,531
has to spend one full night cleaning

340
00:11:21,531 --> 00:11:23,538
the headquarters with a mop.

341
00:11:23,718 --> 00:11:25,982
Rosa calls it the Margie shift.

342
00:11:26,162 --> 00:11:28,878
Marjorie passed in twenty twenty-two,

343
00:11:28,878 --> 00:11:30,713
and Rosa gave the eulogy.

344
00:11:30,893 --> 00:11:32,983
She held up a twenty-dollar bill.

345
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:35,880
Here's what I want you to remember,

346
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:36,316
honey.

347
00:11:36,496 --> 00:11:38,923
Everybody's kind to the boss.

348
00:11:39,103 --> 00:11:41,114
What matters is how you treat the

349
00:11:41,114 --> 00:11:42,516
person holding the mop.

350
00:11:42,696 --> 00:11:43,764
Because one day,

351
00:11:43,764 --> 00:11:46,167
you might find out who's holding it.

352
00:11:46,347 --> 00:11:48,038
Tell me in the comments,

353
00:11:48,038 --> 00:11:50,643
sweetheart, how do the people at your

354
00:11:50,643 --> 00:11:52,756
work treat the cleaning staff?

355
00:11:52,936 --> 00:11:55,337
There are more of my family's stories

356
00:11:55,337 --> 00:11:57,608
in the playlist right there on your

357
00:11:57,608 --> 00:11:59,620
screen, and I'll see you in the

358
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,204
next one.
